{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# V2 — Section 4: Analysis & Data Saving\n`Run_SCEE.py` (all inline)","x":-220,"y":-960,"width":440,"height":120,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"inputs","type":"text","text":"### Inputs\n- `df1` — `dipole_l`, `dipole_m`, `dipole_h` per config (from Section 3)\n- `num1`, `num2`, `num3` — actual scaled charge values used in Gaussian\n- `mu_Vacuum`, `PCM1`, `PCM2` — reference dipoles (from Section 2)\n- `gas_dipole` — experimental gas-phase dipole (hardcoded)\n- `dipole_model` — FF vacuum dipole\n- `Model_Dipole`, `Epsilon` — FF liquid dipole + model ε","x":-220,"y":-800,"width":440,"height":360,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"scee_fit","type":"text","text":"### SCEE Self-Consistency Fitting (inline, per config)\nFor each row in `df1`:\n1. Fit quadratic through `(num1, dipole_l)`, `(num2, dipole_m)`, `(num3, dipole_h)`\n2. Solve `a·μ² + (b−1)·μ + c = 0` for self-consistent `muL_SCEE`\n3. If `a < 1e-6` → fallback to linear: `μ = −c / (b−1)`\n\nAlso applied to Vacuum, PCM1, PCM2 to recover `muG`, `mu_Vacuum`, `PCM1`, `PCM2` self-consistently.","x":-220,"y":-400,"width":440,"height":340,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"mu_liquid","type":"text","text":"### Liquid Dipole Calculation (per config)\n`delta_mu = (mu_SCEE × (PCM1 / PCM2)) − mu_Vacuum`\n`mu_liquid = delta_mu + gas_dipole`\n\n`PCM1/PCM2` ratio corrects for incomplete dielectric environment of finite cluster.","x":-220,"y":-20,"width":440,"height":220,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"dipole_liquid","type":"text","text":"### `get_dipole_model_liquid()` (called per replica)\n`gromacs.tools.Dipoles` on production trajectory → `Dipole2.txt`\nExtracts `Model_Dipole` (avg liquid FF dipole) from line 8.\nExtracts `Epsilon` (model dielectric constant) from last line.\n\nUsed for dielectric constant correction and results table.","x":-220,"y":240,"width":440,"height":320,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"collection","type":"text","text":"### Results Collection DataFrame\nOne row per molecule per T/P. Includes:\n- Simulation params: T, P, replicas, config counts (total + filtered)\n- Charge scaling: qr1/2/3, num1/2/3\n- Dipoles: gas, vacuum model, liquid model, mu_Vacuum, PCM1, PCM2, muL_SCEE, delta_mu, mu_liquid\n- Statistics: mean, std (ddof=1), stderr across replica means\n- Optional ε correction: `n² + (mu_liquid/Model_Dipole) × (Model_ε + 1)` if `mu_liquid > Model_Dipole`\n\n→ `Results_{central}.csv`","x":-220,"y":1620,"width":440,"height":440,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"iqr","type":"text","text":"### `write_filtered_data(k=2.0)`\nFor each `Dipole_Calculations.csv` across all replica/T/P dirs:\n- Compute Q1, Q3, IQR of `mu_liquid`\n- Lower = Q1 − k×IQR, Upper = Q3 + k×IQR\n- Rows outside bounds → `muL_SCEE`, `delta_mu`, `mu_liquid` set to NaN\n- Requires ≥ 5 finite values to filter\n→ writes `Dipole_Calculations_filtered.csv`","x":-220,"y":620,"width":440,"height":300,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"plot1","type":"text","text":"### `plot_dipoledist(central, k=2.0)`\n1. Collect all `mu_liquid` across replica CSVs\n2. IQR outlier detection\n3. Histogram: kept (purple), outliers (orange)\n4. Overlay fitted Gaussian curve (teal)\n5. Save → `dipole_distribution_{central}.png/.pdf`\n\n⚠️ Saves to hardcoded absolute path: `~/Research/SCEE_Project/Results/Aromatics_Chapter/figures/`","x":-680,"y":1080,"width":400,"height":360,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"plot2","type":"text","text":"### `plot_dipoledist_filtered(central, k=2.0)`\nSame as `plot_dipoledist` but with additional axis intelligence:\n- Trim axis where Gaussian curve drops below 0.1% of peak\n- Detect histogram gaps (zero-count bins > 3 wide) → trim axis\n- Extend axis to show mild outliers within 2σ of mean\n\n⚠️ Axis limit heuristics can produce sub-optimal results in some cases — flagged for future fix.\n⚠️ Same hardcoded absolute output path.","x":200,"y":1080,"width":400,"height":420,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"outputs","type":"text","text":"### Outputs\n- `Dipole_Calculations_filtered.csv` (per replica dir)\n- `dipole_distribution_{central}.png/.pdf`\n- `dipole_distribution_{central}_filtered.png/.pdf`\n- `dipole_stats_{central}.csv`, `_filtered.csv`\n- `Results_{central}.csv`","x":-220,"y":2160,"width":440,"height":260,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"note1","type":"text","text":"📝 Standard deviation and standard error are computed from per-replica means — not the full config pool. Individual configs within a replica are correlated so treating them as independent would underestimate uncertainty.","x":-220,"y":2480,"width":440,"height":160,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"note2","type":"text","text":"📝 The ε correction formula (`n² + (mu_liquid/Model_Dipole) × (Model_ε + 1)`) is noted in the code as needing clarification with Miguel/Leo. Applied only when `mu_liquid > Model_Dipole`.","x":-220,"y":2700,"width":440,"height":160,"color":"2"}
	],
